    "narrative": "LawDog faces a critical slate today, anchored by **Lawrence Butler**, who leads the team with a 69.61 score. While the lineup remains pending, the combination of a favorable matchup against Mahle and a massive +13% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage makes **Lawrence Butler** our primary engine for power and production. We are also leaning heavily into **Daulton Varsho** (64.82) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (64.13). **Daulton Varsho** benefits significantly from a favorable platoon matchup against Burrows, while **Geraldo Perdomo** capitalizes on an aggressive #2 spot in the order. Meanwhile, **Bryson Stott** (60.17) is an intriguing start; while his raw platoon numbers against a lefty are typically suppressed, he earns a massive boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which creates an ideal environment for his speed profile to impact the scarce stolen base category.\n\nOn the bench, **Taylor Ward** represents our most difficult exclusion, posting a 53.39 score but ultimately falling behind the higher-upside profiles of our starters. While **Taylor Ward** secures a +10% boost for hitting at the top of the order, he suffers a -9% penalty due to platoon dynamics against Soriano, limiting his ceiling in a day where we require maximum efficiency. We continue to monitor the IL closely, with **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Dylan Beavers** remaining sidelined, while **Luis Arraez** is confirmed out of the lineup today, removing any temptation to force him into the fold.\n\nRisks for today include the reliance on \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for key contributors like **Lawrence Butler**. Furthermore, **Cal Raleigh** (49.29) is a marginal play against Ashcraft; while he maintains a #2 spot, he faces an -13% penalty due to the opposing starter\u2019s skill level. We are also keeping a close eye on **Jeremiah Jackson** (49.02), who faces a difficult path to production given an #8 hole in the lineup. Our overall strategy remains 